{"session_id":"svc-1778085769272302142","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-06T16:42:53.73085759Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","resolved_harness":"codex","harness_source":"auto_route","resolved_model":"gpt-5.4-mini","work_dir":"/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-61668fd3-20260506T164248-2d590620","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead inside an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the completion contract — every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file you can point to after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The bead is too big when any of these holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs as separate top-level deliverables.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized sub-pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across more than ~5 files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, treat Step 0 as a split-first pass and favor child-bead scoping before implementation.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, decomposed children may split once more, and third-level splits must be rejected with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose — do not attempt the work:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child slice (focused title, description, AC; copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;` so the decomposition is visible.\u0026#xA;4. Write `.ddx/executions/20260506T164248-2d590620/no_changes_rationale.txt` listing each child ID and slice, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;A clean decomposition is a successful attempt. Do not mix partial implementation with decomposition.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC against concrete evidence (test name, file path, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `.ddx/executions/20260506T164248-2d590620/no_changes_rationale.txt` (what is done, what blocks, what a follow-up needs) before exiting. No commit and no rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`. A well-justified no_changes beats a bad commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If you write `.ddx/executions/20260506T164248-2d590620/no_changes_rationale.txt`, it MUST carry one of:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;one-line shell command\u0026gt;` — the loop runs it (cwd = project root, 60s); exit 0 closes the bead, non-zero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: needs_investigation` + `reason: \u0026lt;why\u0026gt;` — bead stays open for triage.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Bare rationales (\u0026#34;nothing to do\u0026#34;) are rejected.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Freestanding artifacts (investigation reports, findings docs) go under `.ddx/executions/20260506T164248-2d590620/` (the per-attempt evidence directory under `.ddx/executions/`). **Never write reports to `/tmp` or any path outside the repository** — out-of-repo paths are invisible to the post-merge reviewer and cause BLOCK on missing evidence. If the bead names a specific in-repo path, use it; else default to `.ddx/executions/20260506T164248-2d590620/\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md`. Stage and commit the report alongside code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Bead overrides project defaults\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The bead description and AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and conservative project defaults (YAGNI, DOWITYTD, no-docs-unless-asked) in this worktree — write whatever the bead asks for.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized; running it corrupts the bead queue.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other project-instructions files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator — do not keep exploring or testing.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-61668fd3\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eRename Fizeau native harness identity from agent to fiz\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nPROBLEM\u0026#xA;DDx is removing the term `agent` from its public and internal task-execution surfaces except where it literally means an external AI agent. Fizeau still exposes its native execution path as harness `agent` in code, tests, docs, progress fixtures, and contract prose. That makes downstream DDx specs confusing because `agent` can mean the old DDx CLI namespace, Fizeau native loop, or a real external coding agent.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ROOT CAUSE WITH FILE:LINE\u0026#xA;The public contract and service request still document native-only behavior as Harness==\u0026#34;agent\u0026#34; in service.go:609-620. CONTRACT-003 selection docs at docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-003-fizeau-service.md:424-437 still describe hard `Harness` pins but do not reserve `agent` for real external agents or name the native Fizeau harness as `fiz`. Historical rename planning in docs/helix/02-design/plan-2026-04-08-rename-agent.md:143-164 discusses temporary aliases, but the downstream DDx decision for this work is remove, not deprecate.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX\u0026#xA;Make `fiz` the public/native Fizeau harness identity across CONTRACT-003, the root facade comments, native harness registration, CLI/help text, route-status/list-models output, tests, and committed cassettes/fixtures as needed. Remove public `agent` native-harness aliases rather than adding deprecation shims. Keep the word `agent` only where it refers to a real external AI agent concept, historical artifact text that cannot be changed safely, or third-party standards language.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;NON-SCOPE\u0026#xA;Do not rename DDx commands or DDx packages in this repo. Do not alter routing scoring, provider eligibility, quota behavior, or model catalog contents except where tests/fixtures must be renamed from `agent` to `fiz`. Do not add a compatibility alias for `agent` unless a later bead explicitly changes the no-deprecation policy.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;In-scope files include:\u0026#xA;- service.go\u0026#xA;- service_models.go and service_routing.go/native harness registration call sites as needed\u0026#xA;- agentcli/ and cmd/fiz/ help or command text if they expose native harness names\u0026#xA;- docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-003-fizeau-service.md\u0026#xA;- docs/helix/02-design/primary-harness-capability-baseline.md\u0026#xA;- tests/fixtures/cassettes that assert `agent` as the native harness identity\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Out-of-scope files:\u0026#xA;- DDx repository files under ../ddx\u0026#xA;- benchmark result archives unless an active test fixture requires the rename\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PARENT AND DEPENDENCIES\u0026#xA;Parent: fizeau-06524f43. Dependencies: none.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. `rg -n \u0026#34;Harness==\\\u0026#34;agent\\\u0026#34;|Harness == \\\u0026#34;agent\\\u0026#34;|harness=agent|ListModels\\(.*Harness: \\\u0026#34;agent\\\u0026#34;|Name: \\\u0026#34;agent\\\u0026#34;\u0026#34; service*.go agentcli cmd docs tests internal` returns no active contract/code/test hits except allowlisted historical archive comments.\u0026#xA;2. CONTRACT-003 documents `fiz` as the native Fizeau harness identity and states `agent` is reserved for real external AI-agent concepts, not the native Fizeau route.\u0026#xA;3. Focused tests such as `go test ./... -run \u0026#34;Test(ListModels_harnessFilter|ResolveExecuteRoute|Harness|Native|Fiz)\u0026#34;` pass after updating exact final test names.\u0026#xA;4. `fiz` CLI/list-models/route-status surfaces show the native harness as `fiz`, and explicit `Harness: \u0026#34;fiz\u0026#34;` requests execute through the native loop.\u0026#xA;5. Explicit `Harness: \u0026#34;agent\u0026#34;` no longer selects the native loop and fails with the existing typed unknown/incompatible harness error.\u0026#xA;6. `go test ./...` passes.\u0026#xA;7. `lefthook run pre-commit` passes.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003ephase:build, area:contract, area:harness, area:rename, kind:breaking, downstream:ddx\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-06524f43\" spec-id=\"CONTRACT-003\" base-rev=\"0b6223d9e8f3cadb57b9ebe40d5af12378997f51\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260506T164248-2d590620\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref i